{
  "id": "mssql-from-query-to-system",
  "title": "MSSQL: From Query to SYSTEM",
  "category": "service-drill",
  "source": ["Medtech", "OSCP B", "Tally"],
  "designed_by": "ai-composite",
  "description": "Single-machine MSSQL drill: SQLi or auth → stacked queries → xp_cmdshell enable → reverse shell → SeImpersonate → PrintSpoofer/GodPotato → SYSTEM. Covers impacket-mssqlclient, sqlmap, manual UNION/stacked, xp_cmdshell, PrintSpoofer, GodPotato.",
  "introduction": "This scenario drills the MSSQL-to-SYSTEM path: enable xp_cmdshell, get shell, then Potato. High-frequency OSCP pattern when MSSQL or SQLi is present.",
  "mental_model": "MSSQL as mssql$ = often SeImpersonate. Enable xp_cmdshell, download/execute rev shell, then PrintSpoofer/GodPotato. Stacked queries for SQLi.",
  "key_principles": [
    "sp_configure show advanced + xp_cmdshell enable",
    "xp_cmdshell runs as mssql$ (often has SeImpersonate)",
    "certutil or powershell to download rev shell",
    "PrintSpoofer/GodPotato for SeImpersonate → SYSTEM",
    "sqlmap --os-shell for SQLi to xp_cmdshell"
  ],

